{# One sound beat, appended to `#sfx` (see `render.sfx_beat` and `app._answer_stream`).

   `data-init` runs when datastar sees the element, and an APPENDED element is always a new one --
   which is why this is appended to a sink that is cleared at the start of the stream, rather than
   morphed into place. Two identical consecutive beats (two correct answers) would render identical
   markup, and an idempotent morph leaves the existing element alone: the sound would play once and
   then never again. Appending sidesteps the question entirely.

   No `id`, no class, no text: the element exists to be seen by datastar once and then thrown away
   with the rest of the sink. `aria-hidden` because it is not content -- and the sound itself is
   decoration, since every beat it marks is also a toast in an `aria-live` region. #}
<span aria-hidden="true" data-init="$_sound && document.getElementById('sfx-{{ beat }}')?.play()?.catch(() => {})"></span>
